## Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** Single `game` object; `createRng`/mulberry32 used via `rngFloat`/`rngInt` throughout; `endTurn()` resolves consumption→production→morale→trade→events→hazards→end-check in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** `initMap()` builds 8x8 via seeded `rngFloat`; `canBuild()` checks terrain; but `adjacencyBonus` fields and `getAdjacentTiles()` are never read by any production code — dead data. Score 1.

**F3 (Economy):** production chain data exists (power→water→food etc.) and storage caps/overflow are enforced in `endTurn()`, but building `consumption` (water, power costs) is computed (`powerNeeded`) and only logged — never subtracted from `game.resources`, so output is effectively free. Score 1.

**F4 (Population):** colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job; `getProductionOutput()` reads `colonist.skill` but only for `building.workers`, which no code ever populates; `fatigue` is never read by production. Score 1.

**F5 (Needs):** `endTurn()` computes food/water shortfall and lowers `c.morale`; recovery only via event effects; but `getProductionOutput()` never reads `morale`, so it never changes output. Score 1.

**F6 (Research):** 12 nodes, `canResearch()` enforces prereqs, `doResearch()` deducts costs; but only `resilience_1/2` (storm damage) and `trade_tech` (caravan interval) are actually read elsewhere — 9 of 12 node effects (water_tech, food_tech, industry_1/2, etc.) are unused text. Score 1.

**F7 (Events):** 10 defs in `EVENT_DEFINITIONS`; selection is a shuffled non-repeating deck (`rngShuffle`), not weighted; 6 events have 2 choices with distinct `applyEventEffects` outcomes; `eventCooldown` exists but is moot since `fired` Set permanently excludes each event after one use. Score 1.

**F8 (Trade):** `generateCaravan()` prices from `game.resources[res]` (demandMod) and `globalSupply`; `trade()` handles both buy/sell with limited `offering.quantity`. Score 2.

**F9 (Hazard):** `triggerAshstorm()` fires periodically, severity scales with `game.turn`, `building.damage` reduces `getProductionOutput()`, storm_shelter/resilience research mitigate damage; but `repairBuilding()` has no call site anywhere in the UI — dead code, repair unreachable. Score 1.

**F10 (Save/load):** `saveGame()` serializes full state to textarea; `loadGame()` parses with try/catch and `alert()` on bad JSON. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** both `endGame(false,...)` (pop 0) and `endGame(true,...)` (turn≥60 & pop≥12) reachable in `endTurn()`; `renderEndScreen()` computes multi-factor `score`. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** tab click handler + `render()`; log lines show `Turn ${entry.turn}`; tile tooltips explain terrain/damage; Space/Digit1-5 keyboard shortcuts wired; several panels use `auto-fit` grids for narrow screens (though `.two-column` CSS class itself is unused). Score 2.

**F13 (Dev panel):** `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, prereqs, RNG reproducibility, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 `endTurn()` calls headlessly and prints `getGameHash()`. Score 2.

**G1:** production-yield research nodes (water_tech, food_tech, industry_1/2, etc.) never read in `getProductionOutput()`; only non-yield effects (storm resist, caravan timing) are wired. Score 0.

**G2:** shortage writes real `c.morale -= shortage*10`, but `getProductionOutput()` never reads `morale` — final link absent. Score 1.

**G3:** `triggerAshstorm()` sets `building.damage`, read by `getProductionOutput()` to cut output — real pipeline; but `repairBuilding()` (cost+recovery) has no call site anywhere. Score 2.

**G4:** `generateCaravan()` demandMod reads live `game.resources[res]` via hardcoded <20 threshold; `globalSupply` never drifts (static). Score 2.

**G5:** disease/wanderer choices durably mutate `game.colonists`/`game.resources` via `applyEventEffects`; but `effects.fatigue` and `effects.production` fields are silently no-ops (empty loop / unhandled key) for some branches. Score 3.

